.TH TCPING 1 "September 2026" "tcping 1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tcping \- time a TCP connect/disconnect and report any welcome banner

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tcping
[\-w SECONDS] [\-b SECONDS] [\-\-no\-banner]
.I host port

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tcping
opens a TCP connection to
.IR host : port ,
measures the wall-clock time the connect took, in milliseconds, and immediately closes the connection
again. No data is ever sent to the server.

Right after connecting, and before closing the socket,
.B tcping
takes one brief, passive look at whether the server sent anything unsolicited (a "banner") \- the kind of
greeting line that SSH, FTP, SMTP or POP3 servers send as soon as a client connects, before any request is
made. This is a single non-blocking read with a short timeout, not an interactive session: nothing is sent
back to the server and no further conversation is attempted.

.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I host
Hostname or IP address (IPv4 or IPv6) to connect to.
.TP
.I port
TCP port number to connect to.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-w, \-\-timeout SECONDS
Connect timeout. Default: 5.
.TP
.B \-b, \-\-banner\-wait SECONDS
How long to wait for an unsolicited banner after connecting. Default: 1.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-banner
Skip the banner check entirely; close the socket immediately upon a successful connect.

.SH OUTPUT
On success, prints the elapsed connect time, then either the banner text received or a note that none
arrived within the wait window (omitted entirely if \-\-no\-banner was given):
.RS
.nf
host:port connected in 8.42 ms
banner: (none within 1.0s)
.fi
.RE
On failure, prints the elapsed time until the connection attempt gave up, and the underlying error, to
stderr:
.RS
.nf
host:port failed after 2000.31 ms: timed out
.fi
.RE

.SH EXAMPLES
Time a plain connect (HTTPS servers don't speak first, so no banner is expected):
.RS
.B tcping example.com 443
.RE

Check an SMTP server's greeting and how long the TCP handshake itself takes:
.RS
.B tcping mail.example.com 25
.RE

Confirm a port is closed/filtered, with a short timeout instead of the 5s default:
.RS
.B tcping example.com 9999 \-w 2
.RE

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Connected successfully (with or without a banner).
.TP
.B 1
Could not connect (refused, timed out, unreachable, DNS failure, etc.).
.TP
.B 2
Usage error (missing arguments).

.SH AUTHOR
Chris Pollitt.

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nc (1),
.BR telnet (1),
.BR nmap (1)
